{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":608,"LineContent":"    --ext_Bx 0.005 --forc_Br_min -0.005 --forc_n_curves 30"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":611,"LineContent":"\\noindent In \\code{hysteresis}, the $M(B)$ loop is exported to \\code{hysteresis\\_loop.csv}; in \\code{forc}, to \\code{forc\\_curve.csv}; in \\code{sine}, to \\code{sine\\_field.csv}. In pulse/step modes, \\code{--torque\\_tol} controls the equilibrium criterion and \\code{--t\\_sim\\_full 1} disables early stopping (Appendix~A)."}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":758,"LineContent":"V67 \u0026 FORC protocol implementation: introduction of the First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) field mode (\\code{forc}) with saturation/reversal field parameter control (\\code{--forc\\_Br}, \\code{--forc\\_t\\_sat}, \\code{--forc\\_t\\_rev}), real-time dual-panel video monitoring of the minor reversal loop, and automated export to \\code{forc\\_curve.csv}. \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":820,"LineContent":"V35 \u0026 06/07/2026 \u0026 Documented the implementation of the multi-cycle First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) suite and parameters (\\code{--forc\\_\\allowbreak n\\_curves}, \\code{--forc\\_Br\\_min}, \\code{--forc\\_t\\_sat}, \\code{--forc\\_t\\_ramp\\_down}, \\code{--forc\\_t\\_ramp\\_up}) in \\code{compass.py} V67; updated the parameters table, data logging structures, and usage recipes. \\\\"}

