{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":114,"LineContent":"The simulator supports three lattice geometries (square, triangular, honeycomb); \\textbf{seven} external-field modes: static; First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) mode with sat/reversal field parameter control; pulse with explicit timing (delay $\\Delta t$ $\\to$ field for $t_{\\mathrm{pulse}}$ $\\to$ zero field until equilibrium, with the legacy saturation/plateau criterion if $t_{\\mathrm{pulse}}$ is not given); five-segment hysteresis ($0 \\to +B \\to 0 \\to -B \\to 0 \\to +B$) with linear or log-symmetric spacing; sinusoidal field; and step modes \\code{step\\_pos} ($B{=}0$ for $\\Delta t$, then field kept on) and \\code{step\\_neg} (field from $t{=}0$, removed at $\\Delta t$). It also supports periodic boundary conditions with lattice images; real-time monitoring of the alignment order parameter $S \\in [0,1]$; a real-equilibrium criterion (small angular velocity \\emph{and} small mean torque) for pulse/step modes; optional GPU backend through CuPy; MP4 video export, summary images, and CSV time series $(t, B, M, S)$; magnetic-domain visualization through halo coloring; a precomputed dipolar tensor (V40); and performance instrumentation."}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":188,"LineContent":"\\item \\textbf{FORC protocol implementation (V67)}: introduction of the First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) field mode (\\code{forc}) with saturation/reversal field parameter control (\\code{--forc\\_Br}, \\code{--forc\\_t\\_sat}, \\code{--forc\\_t\\_rev}), real-time dual-panel video monitoring of the minor reversal loop, and automated export to \\code{forc\\_curve.csv}."}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":439,"LineContent":"\\code{--field\\_mode} \u0026 \\code{static} \u0026 --- \u0026 External field mode (\\code{static}, \\code{hysteresis}, \\code{sine}, \\code{pulse}, \\code{step\\_pos}, \\code{step\\_neg}, \\code{forc}). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":440,"LineContent":"\\code{--forc\\_n\\_curves} \u0026 30 \u0026 --- \u0026 Number of reversal curves in the FORC suite (default: 30; V67). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":441,"LineContent":"\\code{--forc\\_Br\\_min} \u0026 auto \u0026 T \u0026 Minimum reversal field $B_{r,\\mathrm{min}}$ (default: $-B_{\\mathrm{ext}}$; V67). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":442,"LineContent":"\\code{--forc\\_t\\_sat} \u0026 0.05 \u0026 s \u0026 Saturation hold time per cycle (V67). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":443,"LineContent":"\\code{--forc\\_t\\_ramp\\_down} \u0026 0.10 \u0026 s \u0026 Ramp down time to reversal field per cycle (V67). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":444,"LineContent":"\\code{--forc\\_t\\_ramp\\_up} \u0026 0.20 \u0026 s \u0026 Ramp up sweep time back to saturation per cycle (V67). \\\\"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":604,"LineContent":"\\noindent\\textbf{(7) forc} --- First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) suite. The system simulates a complete family of first-order reversal curves. Each cycle saturates the array at $+B_{\\max}$, ramps down to a reversal field $B_{r, k}$ (spaced evenly from $+B_{\\max}$ to the minimum reversal field \\code{--forc\\_Br\\_min}), and sweeps back to $+B_{\\max}$. The sweep is repeated for a total of \\code{--forc\\_n\\_curves} cycles. Timing is automatically calculated so that the total time is $t_{\\mathrm{sim}} = N_{\\mathrm{curves}} \\cdot (t_{\\mathrm{sat}} + t_{\\mathrm{ramp\\_down}} + t_{\\mathrm{ramp\\_up}})$. The entire suite of curves is logged to \\code{forc\\_curve.csv} containing the reversal field $B_r$ as a fifth column:"}
{"File":"/Users/jps/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/simula agulhas/project_report.tex","LineNumber":606,"LineContent":"# Run a family of 30 FORC curves, sweeping Br down to -5 mT"}
